{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}
{#
  THE ONE PLACE A NOMINEE IS ASKED ANYTHING — /n/confirm/{token}

  Somebody else has entered this person's name into a public award. This page is the
  only point at which they are asked whether that is all right, and whoever opens it is
  by definition not signed in and may never have heard of this platform.

  So three things are load-bearing:

  · BOTH ANSWERS ARE BUTTONS. "Yes" as a button and "No" as grey text is the pattern
    this codebase's cookie notice exists to forbid, and the stakes here are higher than
    analytics — it is whether a named person appears in a public award. The two carry
    an identical class string and differ only in their accent.

  · IT WORKS WITH NO JAVASCRIPT. Two plain POSTs. A privacy or consent control that
    needs JavaScript is missing for exactly the people most likely to block it, and this
    arrives as an SMS link opened in whatever browser the phone defaults to.

  · NOTHING IS PREFILLED ABOUT THEM BEYOND WHAT THE NOMINATOR ALREADY KNEW. The page
    shows the nominator's name and the award, because that is what makes the request
    legible. It does not show the reason written about them: that is a third party's
    words, it is not yet moderated, and a page anybody with the link can open is not
    where it belongs.
#}


{% block content %}
<div class="nc">
  <div class="nc__card">
    <p class="nc__kicker">Africa GATES</p>
    <h1 class="nc__h1">Did {{ nominator }} nominate you?</h1>

    <p class="nc__lede">
      <strong>{{ nominator }}</strong> has put your name forward
      {% if award %}for <strong>{{ award }}</strong>{% else %}for an award{% endif %}.
      Before it goes any further we need to hear from you.
    </p>

    <dl class="nc__facts">
      <div><dt>Your name, as entered</dt><dd>{{ nominee }}</dd></div>
      {% if category %}<div><dt>Category</dt><dd>{{ category }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
      <div><dt>Nominated by</dt><dd>{{ nominator }}</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="nc__ask">By saying yes you confirm you are a real person and that you are
      happy for your name to appear in this award. Your phone number and email are not
      published.</p>

    {#
      Two forms rather than one with two submit buttons. A `<form>` inside a `<form>` is
      silently DELETED by the parser — its children survive and post to the outer action
      — which has shipped three times here. These are siblings.
    #}
    <div class="nc__answers">
      <form method="post" action="/n/confirm/{{ token }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
        <button class="nc__btn nc__btn--yes" type="submit" name="answer" value="yes">
          Yes, that is me
        </button>
      </form>

      <form method="post" action="/n/confirm/{{ token }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
        <button class="nc__btn nc__btn--no" type="submit" name="answer" value="no">
          No, take it down
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <p class="nc__fine">
      Saying no removes the nomination and stops us contacting you about it.
      The link works for {{ ttl_days }} days from when the nomination was made.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
